# Conventional Commits (required)

All commits and **PR titles** must follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/). release-please on `main` uses these messages for semver and `CHANGELOG.md`.

## Format

```
<type>[optional scope]: <short description>

[optional body]

[BREAKING CHANGE: ...]
```

## Types (use one)

| Type | When |
|------|------|
| `feat` | User-visible feature |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `ci` | CI/CD, workflows |
| `chore` | Maintenance, deps, tooling (no user impact) |
| `refactor` | Code change, same behavior |
| `test` | Tests only |
| `build` | Build system |
| `perf` | Performance |

**Breaking:** `feat!:` in title or `BREAKING CHANGE:` in body → major bump.

## Squash merge = PR title matters

PRs merge to **`main`** with squash. The **PR title** becomes the commit release-please reads. Do not use vague titles like `Updates`, `WIP`, or `Fix stuff`.

## Examples

```
feat(register): prefill household from user_households after login
fix: fail prod db deploy when supabase push errors
ci: add semantic pull request title check
docs: document trunk-based main in CI_CD.md
chore: remove uat branch workflow triggers
```

## Do not

- Manually bump `package.json` `version` (release-please Release PR owns that)
- Merge PRs with non-conventional titles (CI `pr-title` check blocks this)

See `docs/CONTRIBUTING.md` and `commitlint.config.js`.
